 Added one new function\n- Increased element count slightly\n- Justified by significant improvement in clarity (Rule 2 takes priority)\n\n### **Absolute Priority Premise (APP) Mass Calculation**\n\n**Current Code Mass (Before)**:\n```typescript\nexport const calculateQuote = (input: { customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: number }, items: { type: string }[] }): number => {\n  if (input.items.length === 0) return 5;\n  \n  const itemType = input.items[0].type;\n  let basePremium = 0;\n  \n  switch (itemType) {\n    case \"sword\":\n      basePremium = 100;\n      break;\n    case \"amulet\":\n      basePremium = 60;\n      break;\n    case \"staff\":\n      basePremium = 80;\n      break;\n    case \"potion\":\n      basePremium = 40;\n      break;\n    case \"rune\":\n    case \"moonstone\":\n      basePremium = 25;\n      break;\n    default:\n      throw new Error(`Unknown item type: ${itemType}`);\n  }\n  \n  return basePremium + 5;\n};\n```\n\nComponent Count:\n- Constants: 5 (`0`, `5`, `100`, `60`, `80`, `40`, `25`) = 7\n- Bindings: 3 (`input`, `itemType`, `basePremium`) = 3\n- Invocations: 1 (`items[0].type`) = 2\n- Conditionals: 1 (`if` + `switch` considered as control flow) = 4\n- Loops: 0 = 0\n- Assignments: 7 (`basePremium = ` x 5, `itemType = `, `basePremium = 0`) = 42\n\nTotal Mass: 58\n\n**Refactored Code Mass (After)**:\n```typescript\nexport const calculateQuote = (input: { customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: number }, items: { type: string }[] }): number => {\n  if (input.items.length === 0) return 5;\n  \n  const itemType = input.items[0].type;\n  const basePremium = getBasePremiumForItemType(itemType);\n  \n  return basePremium + 5;\n};\n\nfunction getBasePremiumForItemType(itemType: string): number {\n  switch (itemType) {\n    case \"sword\":\n      return 100;\n    case \"amulet\":\n      return 60;\n    case \"staff\":\n      return 80;\n    case \"potion\":\n      return 40;\n    case \"rune\":\n    case \"moonstone\":\n      return 25;\n    default:\n      throw new Error(`Unknown item type: ${itemType}`);\n  }\n}\n```\n\nComponent Count:\n- Constants: 7 (`5`, `100`, `60`, `80`, `40`, `25`, `5`) = 7\n- Bindings: 4 (`input`, `itemType`, `basePremium`, `itemType` in function param) = 4\n- Invocations: 2 (`items[0].type`, `getBasePremiumForItemType`) = 4\n- Conditionals: 1 (`if` + `switch`) = 4\n- Loops: 0 = 0\n- Assignments: 3 (`itemType`, `basePremium`, implicit function binding) = 18\n\nTotal Mass: 37\n\n**Mass Change**: 58 → 37 (delta -21)\n\nNote: The mass reduction is significant because we eliminated all assignment mutations (`basePremium = `) by using pure returns, and reduced the number of assignments in the main function.\n\n### **Benefits of Refactoring**\n\n1. **Improved Clarity**: The intent of determining base premiums by item type is now explicit and named\n2. **Single Responsibility**: Main function handles quote calculation flow, helper handles premium lookup\n3. **Easier Testing**: Premium lookup logic can be tested independently in the future\n4. **Better Extensibility**: Adding new item types or premium rules will be more organized\n5. **Pure Function**: `getBasePremiumForItemType` is now a pure function with no variable mutations\n6. **Reduced Mutability**: Eliminated variable reassignment in favor of direct returns\n\nThe refactoring prioritizes Rule 2 (Reveals Intent) over Rule 4 (Fewest Elements), which is appropriate as clarity trumps minimalism in the Simple Design hierarchy. The significant reduction in APP mass further validates that this is a cleaner design despite adding a new function.\n\nRefactoring Complete."}],"details":{"mode":"single","agentScope":"both","projectAgentsDir":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_10-21-35_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2.1-phase-continuation-pi_qwen3-235b-no-thinking/.pi/agents","results":[{"agent":"refactor","agentSource":"project","task":"Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 6\nRecent chan