- Function purpose: \"Calculates insurance quote premium based on items and customer\"\n- Assessment: The name clearly reveals intent and matches the function's responsibility\n- Decision: Keep current name - it accurately describes the function's purpose\n\n**Current Code Mass Calculation:**\n```\nfunction calculateQuote(input: { customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: number }, items: { type: string }[] }): number {\n  const PROCESSING_FEE = 5;  // Constant: 1\n  if (input.items.length === 0) return PROCESSING_FEE;  // Conditional: 4\n  \n  // Check for three-of-a-kind premium (3 runes or 3 moonstones = 60 G)\n  const componentTypes = [\"rune\", \"moonstone\"] as const;  // Binding: 1\n  for (const componentType of componentTypes) {  // Loop: 5\n    const threeOfAKindPremium = getThreeOfAKindPremium(input.items, componentType);  // Invocation: 2, Binding: 1\n    if (threeOfAKindPremium !== null) {  // Conditional: 4\n      return threeOfAKindPremium + PROCESSING_FEE;  // Invocation: 1 (implicit), Conditional: 1 (implicit for return)\n    }\n  }\n\n  // Default calculation: sum of individual item premiums\n  const basePremium = input.items.reduce((sum, item) => {  // Binding: 1, Invocation: 2 (reduce)\n    return sum + getBasePremiumForItemType(item.type);  // Invocation: 2 (getBasePremiumForItemType, +)\n  }, 0);  // Constant: 1\n  \n  return basePremium + PROCESSING_FEE; // Invocation: 1 (implicit), Conditional: 1 (implicit for return)\n}\n```\n\nComponent Count:\n- Constants: 2 (5, 0) = 2\n- Bindings: 4 (PROCESSING_FEE, componentTypes, threeOfAKindPremium, basePremium, componentType, sum, item - but counting unique declarations) = 4\n- Invocations: 5 (getThreeOfAKindPremium, getBasePremiumForItemType, reduce, +, return) = 10\n- Conditionals: 3 (if items.length, if !== null, for loop condition) = 12\n- Loops: 1 (for...of) = 5\n- Assignments: 0 = 0\n\nTotal Mass: 29\n\n**Refactoring Changes:**\nReordered the code to follow a more logical flow:\n1. Early return for empty items