ot insured in the policy -- (non-insured item: claim rejected)\");\n  it.todo(\"should reject claim if damages include more items of a type than insured -- (e.g. two swords damaged but only one insured)\");\n  it.todo(\"should reject claim if damage amount is negative -- (negative amount: claim rejected)\");\n  it.todo(\"should reject quote for unknown item type -- (e.g. type: \\\"broomstick\\\")\");\n\n  it.todo(\"should cap total payout at twice the insurance sum -- (cap = 2 × insurance sum)\");\n  it.todo(\"should reduce cap by payout amount after each claim -- (first claim reduces cap for second)\");\n  it.todo(\"should exhaust cap after two 1500 G claims on a policy with sword (1000 G) insurance -- (first claim: 1400 G, remaining cap 600 G; second claim: 600 G payout, cap 0 G)\");\n\n  it.todo(\"should round final payout down to whole G in MHPCO's favor -- (350.5 G → 350 G)\");\n});\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784975138757},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"chatcmpl-tool-bdbde451f975755d","name":"grep","arguments":{"pattern":"export const calculateQuote","path":"src/claim-office.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"nebius/qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-instruct-2507","usage":{"input":2939,"output":32,"cacheRead":6624,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":9595,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784975138757,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-320e1a38-86c9-492a-8d25-40ca2155acf4","responseModel":"Qwen/Qwen3-235B-A22B-Instruct-2507"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"chatcmpl-tool-bdbde451f975755d","toolName":"grep","content":[{"type":"text","text":"claim-office.ts:1: export const calculateQuote = (input: { customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: number }, items: { type: string, cursed?: boolean, enchantment?: number }[] }): number => {"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784975139382},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Refactoring: Applying Four Rules of Simple Design\n\n### Step 1: Naming Evaluation (Rule 2)\n\n**Naming Evaluation**:\n- Current name: `calculateQuote`\n- Function purpose: \"calculates insurance premium for magical items, applying base premiums, surcharges for cursed/enchanted items, three-of-a-kind bonuses, and processing fee\"\n- Question: Does \"calculateQuote\" clearly reveal this intent?\n- Assessment: The name is acceptable but could be more specific. However, it's already descriptive enough for the current functionality.\n- Decision: Keep current name because it clearly conveys the main purpose.\n\n### Step 2: Calculate Initial APP Mass\n\n**Current Code Mass**:\n```typescript\nexport const calculateQuote = (input: { customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: number }, items: { type: string, cursed?: boolean, enchantment?: number }[] }): number => {\n  const PROCESSING_FEE = 5;\n  if (input.items.length === 0) return PROCESSING_FEE;\n\n  const basePremium = input.items.reduce((sum, item) => {\n    return sum + getBasePremiumForItemType(item.type, item.cursed, item.enchantment);\n  }, 0);\n  \n  const componentTypes = [\"rune\", \"moonstone\"] as const;\n  for (const componentType of componentTypes) {\n    const threeOfAKindPremium = getThreeOfAKindPremium(input.items, componentType);\n    if (threeOfAKindPremium !== null) {\n      return threeOfAKindPremium + PROCESSING_FEE;\n    }\n  }\n\n  return basePremium + PROCESSING_FEE;\n};\n\nfunction getBasePremiumForItemType(itemType: string, cursed: boolean | undefined, enchantment: number | undefined): number {\n  let basePremium = 0;\n  switch (itemType) {\n    case \"sword\":\n      basePremium = 100;\n      break;\n    case \"amulet\":\n      basePremium = 60;\n      break;\n    case \"staff\":\n      basePremium = 80;\n      break;\n    case \"potion\":\n      basePremium = 40;\n      break;\n    case \"rune\":\n    case \"moonstone\":\n      basePremium = 25;\n      break;\n    default:\n      throw new Error(`Unknown item type: ${itemType}`);\n  }\n\n  if (cursed) {\n    basePremium += Math.ceil(basePremium * 0.5);\n  }\n\n  if (enchantment !== undefined && enchantment >= 5) {\n    basePremium += Math.ceil(basePremium * 0.3);\n  }\n\n  return basePremium;\n}\n\nfunction getThreeOfAKindPremium(items: { type: string, cursed?: boolean, enchantment?: number }[], itemType: string): number | null {\n  const matchingItems = items.filter(item => item.type === itemType);\n  if (matchingItems.length === 3) {\n    return 60;\n  }\n  return null;\n}\n```\n\nComponent Count:\n- Constants: 4 (`PROCESSING_FEE`, \"rune\", \"moonstone\", 60 in `getThreeOfAKindPremium`) = 4\n- Bindings: 12 (`input`, `PROCESSING_FEE`, `basePremium` (2×), `sum`, `item`, `componentTypes`, `componentType`, `threeOfAKindPremium`, `itemType`, `cursed`, `enchantment`, `matchingItems`) = 12\n- Invocations: 7 (`calculateQuote`, `reduce`, `getBasePremiumForItemType`, `getThreeOfAKindPremium`, `filter`, `Math.ceil` ×2) = 14\n- Conditionals: 5 (`if` empty items, `if` cursed, `if` enchantment, `if` threeOfAKindPremium !== null, `if` matchingItems.length === 3) = 20\n- Loops: 2 (`reduce`, `for...of`) = 10\n- Assignments: 4 (`basePremium = 0`, `basePremium = 100` etc., `basePremium +=` ×2) = 24\n\nTotal Mass: 84\n\n### Step 3: Apply Simple Design Rules (in order)\n\n#### Rule 1: Tests Pass\nAll 12 existing tests pass. This is verified by the fact that we're at the refactor phase with 12 passing tests.\n\n#### Rule 2: Reveals Intent\nThe code structure is generally clear, but there are opportunities to improve readability:\n- The `getBasePremiumForItemType` function handles multiple concerns (base premium, cursed surcharge, enchantment surcharge)\n- The three-of-a-kind logic returns early, which is good, but the loop over component types could be clearer\n- Early return for empty items is good for clarity\n\n#### Rule 3: No Duplication\n- No obvious duplication in the code\n- The surcharge calculations in `getBasePremiumForItemType` follow a similar pattern but for different conditions\n- No conceptual duplication detected\n\n#### Rule 4: Fewest Elements\n- The code has 3 functions which is reasonable for the complexity\n- Some simplifications might be possible without sacrificing clarity\n\n### Step 4: Implement Refactoring\n\nI'll make the following improvements:\n\n1. Extract the surcharge calculations into separate functions for better clarity\n2. Reorganize the component types array to be a constant at the top level\n3. Simplify the three-of-a-kind premium calculation to avoid the loop\n\nThese changes prioritize Rule 2 (reveals intent) while not increasing complexity.\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b9e06f2fbb19829d","name":"edit","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.ts","edits":[{"oldText":"export const calculateQuote = (input: { customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: number }, items: { type: string, cursed?: boolean, enchantment?: number }[] }): number => {\n  const PROCESSING_FEE = 5;\n  if (input.items.length === 0) return PROCESSING_FEE;\n\n  // Calculate base premium by summing individual item values\n  const basePremium = input.items.reduce((sum, item) => {\n    return sum + getBasePremiumForItemType(item.type, item.cursed, item.enchantment);\n  }, 0);\n  \n  // Check for three-of-a-kind premium (3 runes or 3 moonstones = 60 G)\n  const componentTypes = [\"rune\", \"moonstone\"] as const;\n  for (const componentType of componentTypes) {\n    const threeOfAKindPremium = getThreeOfAKindPremium(input.items, componentType);\n    if (threeOfAKindPremium !== null) {\n      return threeOfAKindPremium + PROCESSING_FEE;\n    }\n  }\n\n  return basePremium + PROCESSING_FEE;\n};","newText":"const COMPONENT_TYPES = [\"rune\", \"moonstone\"] as const;\nconst THREE_OF_A_KIND_BONUS = 60;\nconst PROCESSING_FEE = 5;\n\nexport const calculateQuote = (input: { customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: number }, items: { type: string, cursed?: boolean, enchantment?: number }[] }): number => {\n  if (input.items.length === 0) return PROC