ngth, getBaseItemPremium, getItemPremium, reduce, addCursedSurcharge, addHighEnchantmentSurcharge, Math.ceil, switch) ≈ 10\n- Conditionals: 5+ (if empty, for loop, if cursed, if enchantment, switch) ≈ 5\n- Loops: 2 (for loop, reduce) = 2\n- Assignments: 5+ (premium initialization, multiple premium reassignments) ≈ 5\n\nTotal Mass ≈ (3×1) + (15×1) + (10×2) + (5×4) + (2×5) + (5×6) = 3 + 15 + 20 + 20 + 10 + 30 = 98\n\n*After Refactoring*:\n- Only change was renaming function from `hasThreeOfAKind` to `hasExactlyThreeOfAKind`\n- All component counts remain identical\n- Total Mass ≈ 98 (no significant change)\n\n**Benefits**:\n- Improved code clarity and intent revelation\n- Prevents potential misunderstanding about function behavior\n- Self-documenting name reduces need for comments\n- All tests continue to pass, ensuring behavioral equivalence\n\nThe refactoring focused on Rule 2 (Reveals Intent) since this provides the highest value improvement. The name change makes the function's contract crystal clear - it checks for exactly three items of a kind, not three or more. This prevents potential bugs if the code were ever modified in the future to handle different quantities.\n\nRefactoring Complete."}],"details":{"mode":"single","agentScope":"both","projectAgentsDir":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_10-21-35_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2.1-phase-continuation-pi_qwen3-235b-no-thinking/.pi/agents","results":[{"agent":"refactor","agentSource":"project","task":"Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 14\nRecent changes: Corrected test expectation to match actual implementation - cursed sword and amulet policy should be 215 G total premium (150 G + 60 G + 5 G)\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done.","exitCode":0,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Task: Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 14\nRecent changes: Corrected test expectation to match actual implementation - cursed sword and amulet policy should be 215 G total premium (150 G + 60 G + 5 G)\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done."}],"timestamp":1784975190962},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"chatcmpl-tool-aa5a2a53dd7295be","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.ts"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b73ffc660cf35a9f","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.spec.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"nebius/qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-instruct-2507","usage":{"input":80,"output":63,"cacheRead":6576,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":6719,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784975190982,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-99666694-c023-4fb8-8bd1-75289947218b","responseModel":"Qwen/Qwen3-235B-A22B-Instruct-2507"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"chatcmpl-tool-aa5a2a53dd7295be","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"const COMPONENT_TYPES = [\"rune\", \"moonstone\"] as const;\nconst THREE_OF_A_KIND_BONUS = 60;\nconst PROCESSING_FEE = 5;\n\nexport const calculateQuote = (input: { customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: number }, items: { type: string, cursed?: boolean, enchantment?: number }[] }): number => {\n  if (input.items.length === 0) return PROCESSING_FEE;\n\n  // Check for three-of-a-kind premium (3 runes or 3 moonstones = 60 G)\n  for (const componentType of COMPONENT_TYPES) {\n    if (hasThreeOfAKind(input.items, componentType)) {\n      return THREE_OF_A_KIND_BONUS + PROCESSING_FEE;\n    }\n  }\n\n  // Calculate base premium by summing individual item values\n  const basePremium = input.items.reduce((sum, item) => {\n    return sum + getItemPremium(item);\n  }, 0);\n\n  return basePremium + PROCESSING_FEE;\n};\n\nfunction getBaseItemPremium(itemType: string): number {\n  switch (itemType) {\n    case \"sword\":\n      return 100;\n    case \"amulet\":\n      return 60;\n    case \"staff\":\n      return 80;\n    case \"potion\":\n      return 40;\n    case \"rune\":\n    case \"moonstone\":\n      return 25;\n    default:\n      throw new Error(`Unknown item type: ${itemType}`);\n  }\n}\n\nfunction addCursedSurcharge(premium: number): number {\n  return Math.ceil(premium * 1.5); // 50% surcharge\n}\n\nfunction addHighEnchantmentSurcharge(premium: number): number {\n  return Math.ceil(premium * 1.3); // 30% surcharge\n}\n\nfunction getItemPremium(item: { type: string, cursed?: boolean, enchantment?: number }): number {\n  let premium = getBaseItemPremium(item.type);\n  \n  if (item.cursed) {\n    premium = addCursedSurcharge(premium);\n  }\n  \n  if (item.enchantment !== undefined && item.enchantment >= 5) {\n    premium = addHighEnchantmentSurcharge(premium);\n  }\n  \n  return premium;\n}\n\nfunction hasThreeOfAKind(items: { type: string, cursed?: boolean, enchantment?: number }[], itemType: string): boolean {\n  return items.filter(item => item.type === itemType).length === 3;\n}\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784975191925},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"chatcmpl-tool-b73ffc660cf35a9f","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { calculateQuote, processClaim } from \"./claim-office.js\";\n\ndescribe(\"MHPCO Claim Office\", () => {\n  it(\"should return a premium of 5 G for an empty item list -- (empty list: only processing fee)\", () => {\n    expect(calculateQuote({ customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 }, items: [] })).toBe(5);\n  });\n\n  it(\"should return base premium 100 G for a single sword -- (sword: 1000 G value, 100 G base premium)\", () => {\n    expect(calculateQuote({ \n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 }, \n      items: [{ type: \"sword\" }] \n    })).toBe(105); // Base premium 100 G + 5 G fee = 105 G total premium\n  });\n  it(\"should re