hat should be applied to the policy base premium. However, the order matters for the final rounding. \n\nLet me check the integration example: \"a long-standing customer's second contract with a cursed, highly enchanted sword → premium: 160 G (100 G base + 50 G curse + 30 G high enchantment − 20 G loyalty + 10 G first insurance − 15 G follow-up contract = 155 G + 5 G fee = 160 G)\"\n\nThis shows the modifiers are applied to the base sum, and then the processing fee is added. Let me fix our implementation to apply all modifiers before rounding only the final result:\n\n\n\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"chatcmpl-tool-aaf3ab30cab27dd2","name":"edit","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.ts","edits":[{"oldText":"  // Apply 20% loyalty discount for customers with 2 or more years\n  if (input.customer.yearsWithMHPCO >= LOYALTY_THRESHOLD) {\n    policyBasePremium = policyBasePremium * (1 - LOYALTY_DISCOUNT_PERCENT);\n  }\n\n  // Apply 10% initial assessment surcharge for first insurance\n  // Note: Each item in a quote is treated as a first insurance, regardless of customer history\n  policyBasePremium = policyBasePremium * (1 + FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_PERCENT);\n\n  // Round up the final premium in MHPCO's favor\n  // Only round at the very end as per MHPCO rules\n  return Math.ceil(policyBasePremium) + PROCESSING_FEE;","newText":"  let finalPremium = policyBasePremium;\n\n  // Apply 20% loyalty discount for customers with 2 or more years\n  if (input.customer.yearsWithMHPCO >= LOYALTY_THRESHOLD) {\n    finalPremium = finalPremium * (1 - LOYALTY_DISCOUNT_PERCENT);\n  }\n\n  // Apply 10% initial assessment surcharge for first insurance\n  // Note: Each item in a quote is treated as a first insurance, regardless of customer history\n  finalPremium = finalPremium * (1 + FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_PERCENT);\n\n  // Add processing fee\n  finalPremium += PROCESSING_FEE;\n  \n  // Round up the final premium in MHPCO's favor\n  // Only round at the very end as per MHPCO rules\n 